  "custom_firmware": "OVMF X64 RELEASE, 4 MiB. The only firmware source change selects a fixed 1366 by 768 mode in QemuRamfbDxe. The packaged OVMF default control produced 800 by 600. Each trial used separate firmware variables.",
  "failure": "Both first exact-size trials stopped at the byte comparison. QEMU 10.0.13 emitted a 1366 by 768 P6 header followed by 4100 bytes per row. P6 requires 4098. Neither run reached shutdown. The original P6s, memory dumps and logs are preserved.",
  "capture": "New guests used original QMP PNGs. In both guests every Home pixel matched the physical framebuffer in BGRX order. The original QEMU PPMs also matched after each row\u2019s two extra bytes were excluded. The merged distribution F10 reader consumed packed RGB serialized from the PNGs.",
  "scope": "Virtual 1x RAM framebuffer, not a physical laptop or the shipping optical image. No OS product changes or automatic scale selection tested.",
